==Notes==

*When cast against a [[player character]] (PC) or a PC's [[associate]], this spell causes a [[dazed]] effect instead.
**The duration of the daze effect, if at least 4 rounds and the target is a PC, is halved under the normal game [[difficulty setting]], and quartered under easier settings. 
*Merchants under the influence of this spell suffer a -10 penalty to their [[appraise]] skill if they make an opposed skill check when opening their store. This means that prices could be adjusted 10% (of the item's value) in the PC's favor. However, this is subject to a minimum skill of 1, so there is no benefit when the merchant has no (or little) ''appraise'' skill in the first place.
*Due to a .2da bug, ''clarity'' is not an additional [[counterspell]] of this spell.

